2:T63b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average kitchen renovation price range in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a kitchen renovation may typically range from about £5,000 for a limited refresh to £35,000 or more for a larger, higher-specification project. Every property and specification is different, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to renovate a small kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a small kitchen may typically cost roughly £5,000–£20,000, depending on whether the layout stays, which appliances are replaced and the quality of the cabinets, worktops and finishes. Every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to reface kitchen cabinets or replace them?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Refacing or replacing doors can cost less than installing new cabinets, particularly when the existing units are sound and the layout works. It may not address storage needs, damaged carcasses or poor-quality fittings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does changing the kitchen layout increase the renovation cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can. Moving sinks, dishwashers, cookers or radiators may require additional plumbing, electrical work, flooring repairs and wall preparation. Removing walls may also involve structural work and specialist advice."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-renovation-price-range","d"]
